# Regression fixture for inc-mc37 (tanglefoot half). Player::AutoPickupFloor's
# unidentified-magic branch (src/Player.cpp) must NOT auto-stow an EF_MUNDANE
# item -- here a tanglefoot bag -- while it still stows real unidentified magic
# (the rogue-archer's dimension-door potion). Read by
# tools/check_mundane_autopickup.sh.
#
# Route: an orc barbarian; wizard-summon a base human to the east; add the
# "rogue-archer" template, whose gear is a GUARANTEED 1d2 tanglefoot bag
# (lib/mon2.irh) plus a 1d1 dimension-door potion; genocide it so the pile drops
# on one tile; step onto the tile so AutoPickupFloor runs. The tanglefoot bag
# must REMAIN in view (not stowed); the potion must be gone (stowed), proving
# the branch still hoards real magic.
@include chargen.keys
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE
DOWN*9
SPACE
ESC
w
@expect "Wizard Mode Options:"
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "Human"
RIGHT
ENTER
w
@choose "Add Template to Creature"
RIGHT
ENTER
@choose "Rogue-Archer"
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
RIGHT
@dump:before
SPACE
g
@choose "2 tanglefoot bags"
@while "In the Air':2 tanglefoot bags" s
@while "Ready Hand" ESC
@dump:picked
a
@choose "(in pack) 2 tanglefoot bags"
@dump:aim
ENTER
@dump:thrown
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:try1
